{"title":"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Sort_of_Root_Jumping)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Sort of Root Jumping)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab232223b7ae6bf683af4df56df9e3f829bc188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73dbae0d4cab732558228057baa3c3c8b389db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} + b^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />. Show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638b4cdc94bbcb73f856ee953ec1e28be7f7b42a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a^{2} + b^{2}}{ab + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" />\nis the square of an integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24ibl_opV34\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=24ibl_opV34</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wqCdEE1Ueh0\">https://youtu.be/wqCdEE1Ueh0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Choose integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf7b6cca779a019f721133cfd43512c919d9f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/849c51ddf43cf78a36a3460c051d5d981b72bd2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=k(ab+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />\nNow, for fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, out of all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> choose the one with the lowest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d698e771d0c2fd5a9a0a898934d443911dc59a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. Label <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/224e725e1d17fc7c192bfec00feee6736de6b2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;=\\min(a,b), a&#39;=\\max(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adf47d6bca0775c63e74577f57c9afc9d380a58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;^2-kb&#39;a&#39;+b&#39;^2-k=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" /> is a quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1e51ef5511c6d27c703b84edc8ff93ffbc3717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&#39;$\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />. Should there be another root, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51ed22c1a97267ab79560425f4e72e3bcd64dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the root would satisfy: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b22cc9f1d3b5b7c64421b88127023386913add6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;c&#39;\\leq a&#39;c&#39;=b&#39;^2-k&lt;b&#39;^2\\implies c&#39;&lt;b&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"292\" height=\"17\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51ed22c1a97267ab79560425f4e72e3bcd64dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> isn't a positive integer (if it were, it would contradict the minimality condition). But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832a844d7aa27c1c52971605a4c9651b62759d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;=kb&#39;-a&#39;$\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51ed22c1a97267ab79560425f4e72e3bcd64dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;$\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer; hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d217ba8f255ea3a8938e70e98021da78ab599579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;\\leq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />. In addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e1b791754584d80172c56349bb9fc589663a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a&#39;+1)(c&#39;+1)=a&#39;c&#39;+a&#39;+c&#39;+1=b&#39;^2-k+b&#39;k+1=b&#39;^2+(b&#39;-1)k+1\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"620\" height=\"19\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892c347920ff92a20015d2ba1bff0e468e6995b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;&gt;-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. We conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4ae27359c0ecedc2a16e889e5e9d86429d3fb94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&#39;=0$\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f3940a63fa0c45de391fb3e2448b76cadffd7b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&#39;^2=k$\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>This construction works whenever there exists a solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> for a fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is always a perfect square.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Sort_of_Root_Jumping.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Sort_of_Root_Jumping)\">Solution 2 (Sort of Root Jumping)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Sort of Root Jumping)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed by way of contradiction.\n</p><p>WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb57e55bf88090389ea5b582cb7d7af7dbee40c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and fix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> to be the nonsquare positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a4565e202b8876adaeb2efec5e5b982e4c1e2a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2+b^2}{ab+1}=c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"98\" height=\"42\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed208a95af886147b0f43c57cbf6fa0ef54cbc08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=c(ab+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"21\" /> Choose a pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> out of all valid pairs such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is minimized. Expanding and rearranging, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6cace3fb65b06da7dc7211b5d8d6bc72517fce9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(a)=a^2+a(-bc)+b^2-c=0.\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"20\" />\nThis quadratic has two roots, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1f36d3bc6be3fe42e698177780406487ecbbbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a-r_1)(a-r_2)=P(a)=0.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />\nWLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f68d9966df24239f1c1b5fb14de384b5b780aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />. By Vieta's, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b4476042d87d3c43bbbb3efe4d7a53f8a88aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(1) } r_2=bc-a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5ccb6c70478843d1c2f6eb77861d6f8b89bbfb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(2) } r_2=\\frac{b^2-c}{a}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"41\" />\nFrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/f/19f561c1f492153db0c45db3c64494476d65b9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer, because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are integers.\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5faa621f85e5481eaa7ae3c765863574a782c6bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(2)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is nonzero since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not square, from our assumption.\n</p><p>We can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in the original expression, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b190b99505b4c66aef89f6e26e82f10840fbe3e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(r_2)=P(a)=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d875725f6aeda01133d11cde95d9db994be0308.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{r^2_2+b^2}{r_2b+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"93\" height=\"44\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf620f4f9ec64e55a21bbc12fc2be119cc47046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c112cb55bb4637244ecf7abd7ff541d59d9f208c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2b+1&gt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41de41365de4105db94ec7c0fac5bf1efd72dc0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2b+1\\neq{0},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/0/b207c4f0ca41d8e208e5de384afbe1c5b0dac138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;0, r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> is a positive integer. \n</p><p>We construct the following inequalities: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2adf59d280eca0384ead3cc0bd09ef3a624812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2=\\frac{b^2-c}{a}&lt;a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is positive. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f35f3bc2d2df9ca6914429262423e31068d445a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2+b&lt;a+b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" /> contradicting the minimality of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f588b95d2616ba65d936e39966057315d60dc23f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the given expression be equal to the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. We rearrange the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf4958a6286321b9a55acc62b6cefe6c86f6616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2 = k(ab+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" /> and complete the square for the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to transform the problem into the study of a Generalized Pell Equation. By multiplying by 4 and grouping terms, we arrive at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e4ffaa3eaf398d743ce6d9ee2f2150924185cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2a - kb)^2 - (k^2 - 4)b^2 = 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7990f8429cdf54258566bf99d084de2f769e68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = |2a - kb|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c3e10b062b5ba2bbe375a669d09bb690d3a66b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eeb4c21af3d09692c0c09a6600d1ab2e4d3cc3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = k^2 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, which yields the following equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b90a5bf4698685e7e670a260b81f649d875e5e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[X^2 - DY^2 = 4k\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is not a perfect square, then for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bb76208dae30e44513fa10ff49ba1329094713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, the discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive non-square integer, allowing us to use the theory of Pell equations. The associated unit equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408cd18f112e759ec2ef5e1cfa22cdebf75e69a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u^2 - Dv^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /> has the fundamental solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d01594f962022cad1c0ccc93fc68e63fcdf479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />, which corresponds to the algebraic unit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe4d18c3b550e642fc7187ccc03729ae3a12af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon = \\frac{k - \\sqrt{D}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"43\" />. We can generate a strictly smaller integer solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a32ccb19729cba543c2de1d1e763582876f5c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(X&#39;, Y&#39;)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> from any solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158fccfef8b9c1a61a13ba579c3a32ec090c9cb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(X, Y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6c71bed9556a4ab9e26ba6b5cc41713d885d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y^2 &gt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> by applying this unit, where the new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-coordinate is defined below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e252af2ef9b80254fee6c4d6a12db1a20f6efe6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Y&#39; = \\left| \\frac{kY - X}{2} \\right|\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"44\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e4c05ab47cb5214a327a1b50d2318d3870f2194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X^2 \\equiv k^2Y^2 \\pmod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"21\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d6051138ab392b872560f1e816f5a417d03b5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X \\equiv kY \\pmod 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f898155997022cd6259c6a0e0b50802954d80122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is always an integer, and algebraic manipulation confirms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/3007484cdedc8c18859e915d2de7ebae019ca02b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y&#39; &lt; Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6c71bed9556a4ab9e26ba6b5cc41713d885d3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y^2 &gt; k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />. Because a sequence of decreasing non-negative integers must terminate, we must eventually reach a solution where the descent step yields zero, specifically <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4e42c7f87f108f11760a8df2da87dec1b73aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y&#39; = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22be463391a558756326ba71492fe4275d4ba469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kY = X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />, and substituting this back into the Pell equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed2065e036fd363c4c21cf5d234d5a95271e8a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(kY)^2 - (k^2 - 4)Y^2 = 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"21\" />. This simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a8c394c4f9b547a525e810e648bbfddaf94294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4Y^2 = 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8cbc0738b2c93d094d9525118c8805c5010cd90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y^2 = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"17\" />, which proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let some fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> equal the given expression such that there is at least one valid solution. Choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651d2c305c3854c940bc46b1eb5856126ff1e6dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)=(A,B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> out of all possible solutions such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b831312585cb4ab6697896f86b72accbddbc4b45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is minimized, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89abb56312bfa56beefafdcf38e149c5110b4a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\ge B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> without loss of generality. By definition,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8ad91bf38b109f50b8f7adc5b057840a3102ebd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{A^2+B^2}{AB+1}=k \\implies A^2 - (kB)A + (B^2-k) = 0 \\text{,}\\]\" width=\"374\" height=\"41\" /> therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a root of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/90584a1da8b7a7220f9c8ca7c7ffe52503b4292b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^2 - (kB)x + (B^2-k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the other root.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/25175d0e269ed8d27eef5420fe041de8f3941aa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b04147078958e72c415bb66097eda5894ae94dd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Claim 1: } r \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\ge 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Per Vieta's, the sum of the roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/756ffa1fba3d6e866685ed551e68040e8ab3143e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + A = kB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc67527e3ad232a8a721dbb1a29bffea0e59426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, k, B \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\implies r \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />. Moreover,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/20647304168e18800f24fdf05cbc0fb54f13f94c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(r)=0 \\implies r^2 - (kB)r + (B^2-k) = 0 \\implies \\frac{r^2+B^2}{rB+1} = k &gt; 0 \\text{.}\\]\" width=\"514\" height=\"41\" />\nThen, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/93390e53c51c7b49b47efbd84344577d0bab8947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 + B^2 &gt; 0 \\implies rB + 1 &gt; 0 \\implies r &gt; -\\frac{1}{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"349\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f30f6b1b632b15db60332274bb8d817ffc7503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61ccae0b4476d7d25ed24fca6595d239cdc8c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/25175d0e269ed8d27eef5420fe041de8f3941aa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fd8671af98f15bd645d17a11e710f842453b088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Claim 2: } r \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Per Vieta's, the product of the roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf9cea0b8112b985c639f87b73d32d791dd4e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rA = B^2 - k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34d2ddc2e4fded901a090a743ca7eae7fa79cea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A &gt; B \\implies A^2 &gt; B^2 &gt; B^2 - k = rA \\implies rA &lt; A^2 \\implies r + B &lt; A + B \\text{.}\\]\" width=\"560\" height=\"17\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not a positive integer, else <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbdde0ecce1e9fc672fda86fe8fecaed8b0bcb90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r, B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> would be a valid solution to the original expression yet would contradict the minimality condition.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/25175d0e269ed8d27eef5420fe041de8f3941aa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\newline$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/400365c088499af977542271fc6363b086a63499.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/27192dddd2a8e39ba7fe8c2bb1f293401cb15f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rA = B^2 - k \\implies 0 = B^2 - k \\implies k = B^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"346\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the square of an integer, as desired.  — S.A.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=usEQRx4J_ew\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=usEQRx4J_ew</a> ~KevinChen_Yay\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO\" title=\"1988 IMO\">1988 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181043\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.081 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 622/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20988/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.163      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.163      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5412:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017181043 and revision id 291928. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}